# The stage0 compiler's back end: a checked module written as one C file, to
# be linked with the runtime of refined executables
# (semanticscript/compiler/refined/native_runtime.c), which writes output,
# traps with exit code 70, and keeps regions as `refined build --kind
# executable` programs do. The file is:
#
# - a fixed prelude: declarations of the runtime functions it calls, text as a
#   pointer and a length, the checked arithmetic, and lists (a header
#   {length, capacity, data, region, identity} and a data block that starts at
#   four items and doubles, allocated in the list's region as the LLVM backend
#   allocates them, so a region's maxBytes is reached at the same call);
# - each record as a struct of its fields (`m_<field>`), each enum as a struct
#   of an `int32_t tag` and either one `int64_t payload` (the narrow layout,
#   when every payload is an integer, a Bool, or an enum without payloads) or
#   one field per payload (`p_<variant>`), the LLVM backend's layouts, so
#   sizes agree; `rl_<Type>` for a type that holds text, which copies the text
#   into a region (as a list does with what it stores, and a return with an
#   output owned by a region); `la_`, `lg_`, and `lt_<List>` for each list's
#   append, get, and getOrTrap;
# - module constants as static C values;
# - each operation as `static ... o_<name>(...)`: it returns its output, or,
#   when it raises, a bool that is true on failure with the output and error
#   written through `ss_out` and `ss_err`. Its values are C locals `v_<name>`,
#   each call that can fail has a flag `f_<call>`, each bounded loop a counter
#   `n_<label>`, each forEach loop a position `i_<label>`, and each label a C
#   label `l_<label>` followed by its steps. A recursive operation counts its
#   depth in `d_<name>` and traps past its maxRecursion;
# - a C `main` that hands the command line to the runtime and returns main's
#   ExitCode.
#
# A jump to a bounded loop header counts the pass when it comes from inside
# the loop (from the header or a block within it) and resets the count (and a
# forEach loop's position) when it enters the loop from outside, the rule the
# LLVM backend follows, so a loop that passes its bound traps in C as it does
# under `refined run`.
#
# This module is generated from a shorter description by a generator kept
# outside the repository; it is ordinary SemanticScript and is edited as such.

emitc is module
emitc purpose "Write a checked stage0 module as one C file"
emitc path emitc
emitc imports standard.string
emitc imports standard.buffer
emitc imports standard.list
emitc imports standard.map
emitc imports standard.math
emitc imports standard.compare
emitc imports standard.logic
emitc imports standard.test
emitc imports lexer
emitc imports syntax
emitc imports model
emitc imports subset
emitc exports emitModule

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- C spellings
CTarget is record
CTarget purpose "How a standard library target is written in C: the text before, between, and after its arguments; or, for a target of the host library, the name refined_host dispatches on, with how many 64-bit slots its arguments and result take"
CTarget typeParameter none
CTarget field text String
CTarget field before String
CTarget field between String
CTarget field after String
CTarget field host Bool
CTarget field key String
CTarget field slots Int64
CTarget field results Int64

CType is record
CType purpose "How a built-in type is written in C"
CType typeParameter none
CType field text String
CType field cType String

cTargets is table
cTargets purpose "The C spelling of every standard library target of the subset, in the order of subset's builtinTargets"
cTargets rowType CTarget
